/-!
# Candidate coordinates for the two binary G₂ cycle factors

These are finite witness data, with no unproved identities attached. They were
obtained from the actual-root exploratory GAP calculation retained in
`Scratch/G2CycleFiltration/GenerateCandidates.g`. The first 32 rows of the
adapted basis are its proposed submodule basis; standard unit vectors, in
increasing order, complete that basis. The two diagonal blocks of the
conjugated row-action matrices are transposed here to use Lean's column action.

Root matrices in the calculation come from the attributed ATLAS ports
`G2/RootLinearMaps.lean` and `G2/WeylMaps.lean`, revision
8eabb35afe2b5e45bf913a2d05c53e558d2e2917 (copyright 2026 Gerald Höhn and the
ATLAS contributors; `LICENSES/ATLAS.txt`). No assertion about the actual
cycle kernel, invariant subspaces, or irreducibility follows from these data
alone. Separate proofs must establish all such assertions.

Source application: Aschbacher–Smith G.7.2(3), printed p.348 / PDF p.359.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace G2DerivedPermutationFiltration.CycleData

abbrev Half := Fin 32 → ZMod 2

/-- Decode a binary row. The least significant bit has index zero. -/
def bit (r : ℕ) (j : ℕ) : ZMod 2 := if r.testBit j then 1 else 0

